    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Engine TTFT p95, by consumer",
      "description": "Time to first token as the ENGINE measured it: queue wait plus prefill, with no gateway, router or network in it. Compare against 'Mean time to first token, by consumer' above, which is Higress's view of the same moment. Requests that did not come through the gateway carry consumer=\"\" and are excluded here. The label arrives on x-request-id-labels, not SGLang's default x-custom-labels: the router forwards only an allow-list plus the x-request-id- prefix, so the default name is silently dropped. See docs/METRICS-ECOSYSTEM.md.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
