          "legendFormat": "{{consumer}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": false,
          "format": "time_series",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Inter-token latency p95, by consumer",
      "description": "Gap between successive output tokens, per consumer. Nothing else in the stack can produce this: the gateway sees a stream start and a stream end, so a request that stalls halfway through decode looks identical to one that flowed evenly. This is the metric the per-key work was for. Requests that did not come through the gateway carry consumer=\"\" and are excluded here. The label arrives on x-request-id-labels, not SGLang's default x-custom-labels: the router forwards only an allow-list plus the x-request-id- prefix, so the default name is silently dropped. See docs/METRICS-ECOSYSTEM.md.",
