    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Prefix cache hit, by consumer",
      "description": "Share of each consumer's prompt tokens served from the radix cache, derived as 1 - uncached/total. Per-consumer cache behaviour is what decides whether cache_aware routing pays off for them: a consumer with a long stable system prompt should sit near 1, a consumer sending unique prompts near 0. Requests that did not come through the gateway carry consumer=\"\" and are excluded here. The label arrives on x-request-id-labels, not SGLang's default x-custom-labels: the router forwards only an allow-list plus the x-request-id- prefix, so the default name is silently dropped. See docs/METRICS-ECOSYSTEM.md.",
