    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Output token rate, by consumer and replica",
      "description": "Which GPU is doing whose work. The gateway cannot answer this \u2014 it hands every request to one router address and never learns which replica served it \u2014 so this is the only view that ties a consumer to r0 or r1, and the place a routing imbalance shows up per tenant. Requests that did not come through the gateway carry consumer=\"\" and are excluded here. The label arrives on x-request-id-labels, not SGLang's default x-custom-labels: the router forwards only an allow-list plus the x-request-id- prefix, so the default name is silently dropped. See docs/METRICS-ECOSYSTEM.md.",
