    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Edge overhead p95 (gateway minus engine), by consumer",
      "description": "Difference of two p95s from histograms with different bucket edges \u2014 an indicator only, and it can go NEGATIVE, which is an artefact rather than the gateway being faster than the engine. MEASURED TRUTH, from duration_ms - llm_ms per request in gateway.requests over 30 days: p50 1ms, p95 3ms, p99 7ms, max 14ms. The gateway filter chain costs single-digit milliseconds. If this panel shows seconds, it is showing quantile arithmetic, not overhead \u2014 go to the fact table.",
